# LF on every OS, no exceptions for text.
#
# The frontend contract tests regex the SOURCE of public/index.html (and the
# app script inside it) with \n-anchored patterns, and several other suites
# grep source files the same way. A default Windows checkout converts text
# files to CRLF, which broke every one of those tests at once on CI's first
# real Windows run — failures that said nothing about the code. The repo's
# files are authored with LF; this keeps them LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never eol-converted (git usually detects these, but the
# release-critical ones are pinned so a misdetection can't corrupt them).
*.png binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.dmg binary
*.node binary
*.vsix binary
